			<wp:comment_content><![CDATA[Topic:  Chord Theory UI
Hi Michael,
I had a lot of fun learning about all the different chords and scales in Color Piano Theory!
A few enhancements to the UI could make them a lot easier to explore instrumentally.
The current UI plays individual notes for the R, C, or L mouse buttons on the piano keys and the color bars above.

Mouse Key mapping for Black and White Key regions
Left Mouse = individual note
Right Mouse = Major Chord with root at selected key
Center Mouse = Minor Chord with root at selected key
Center Scroll Wheel = Play selected scale starting at selected note, scrolling up or down scale based on scroll speed

The color row above keys (sized taller for easier selection) could be configured by the existing chord selection drop down menu, replicated for Left, Center, and Right.

Adding rows would provide one click access to a wider range of chords.
Enhanced control could add an array of rows that are each configurable with 3 menu bars that define the chords for the left , center, and right mouse.  A single configurable row would add a lot of playful color, but configuring commonly used chords in rows organized by type would make a greater pallet available in a structured format.

Row                         LeftMouse      CenterMouse     RightMouse    
=======================================
free config               
13th                        13b9           min13               13
11th                        11b9            min11               Maj11
9th                          9sus4              min9                 9
7th                          7sus4              min7                 7
6th                          6sus4              min6                 6
chords                     sus4               minb5                Majb5  
=======================================
Piano Keys               SingleNote     Minor                 Major]]></wp:comment_content>
