	<item>
		<title>Promoting your Software</title>
		<link>https://galactic.ink/journal/?p=1312</link>
		<pubDate>Thu, 16 Feb 2012 01:28:27 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[admin]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://mudcu.be/journal/?p=1312</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[You've built it, but somehow, they're not coming... what's a programmer to do? Self-promotion is key. Advertising should only be considered if you've got money burning a hole in your pocket, or after other routes have been expended. I don't claim to be an expert, but have had some great successes over the years, and am here to share what I've learned so far...
<div>
<ul id="internal-source-marker_0.8366455279756337">
	<li>The early bird gets the worm, or, less competition is the best competition.When there is a new space to show off your software, be the 1st!</li>
	<li><a href="http://news.ycombinator.com/">YCombinator</a> is a great place to post news on Technology releases, read their Posting Guidelines. It can produce a good amount of traffic, especially if you hit the front page, which can produce thousands of uniques in a day.</li>
	<li>techcrunch.com, wired.com, smashingmagazine.com?</li>
	<li>Chrome Webstore; creating apps for the Chrome Webstore is a breeze, and the traffic you can get from being featured on their pages is substantial. The community doesn't seem to use the commenting feature much, which is a bummer.</li>
	<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/demos/">Mozillas demos</a>; to get your app on this page, you must release it as MIT open-source or compatible license.</li>
	<li>ChromeExperiments; spectacular resource, the demos being submitted here are amazing.</li>
	<li>Twitter/Facebook/Google+... can we think of an interesting way to display a bunch of HEX values?  We need to make sure when people post our pages, automatically, they look stunning on Facebook and Google+ without the need for them to edit.</li>
	<li>DMOZ, Yahoo Directory, Wikipedia, and other reputable link-farms.</li>
	<li>Design Galleries; <a href="http://bestwebgallery.com/">http://bestwebgallery.com/</a></li>
	<li>Meaningful link-exchanges with other webmaster.</li>
	<li>Include an explanation of the software into a Help screen, and place it in a FoxyBox. This will allow you to target the terms you are looking for, without cluttering the screen.</li>
<ul>
	<li>Metadescription</li>
	<li>Title</li>
</ul>
</ul>
</div>
<div><strong>Promotion</strong> - https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/demos/</div>
<div>

   - Typographic effects

- Breathing galaxies

- Loader.js

- Color Picker(s)

</div>]]></content:encoded>
