			<wp:comment_content><![CDATA[Hey Michael! I wanted to give you some feedback on your Piano Theory in Color! app. 

First of all, this is fucking great. I've wanted something like this for a very long time--a music-learning tool that associates pitch with color. I've been watching the notes pass for about 25 minutes now and I actually feel like I've absorbed some ability. 

May I make one suggestion, though? The name of your app is Piano Theory and you seem to have left out the theory. I strongly suggest that you make your sharps and flats true to the keys and modulations of the compositions or at least give the option. This would breed an entirely new level of comprehension on the user's part. Is this something you think could be done? I guess first I should ask if you understand what I'm talking about (I don't know whether you've studied theory). 

Please let me know if you'd like me to explain more and thanks again for the kick-ass app. For real.

Ian]]></wp:comment_content>
