			<wp:comment_content><![CDATA[Ahh, yes, I’m sure there is some software out there that allows you to connect a physical keyboard to the computer and interact with it, although, I don’t know what that software would be called. I’m planning on adding this functionality at some point in the future, I just need to find the spare time to implement. I love the idea of the app stopping an waiting for the user to input the proper key on the keyboard! Thanks for these great thoughts!

As far as the problem with synesthesia colors being too similar, have you tried the Circle of Fifths mode in Color Piano? One of the major benefits with it is the notes do not look the same next to each-other… notes that are harmonic are similar in color, so the 1st/3rd/5th appear to be analogous. This might be the mode you’re looking for! It was recently added, submitted by a user of Color Piano.

Another thought was to add a “synesthesia” selector to Color Piano that would allow users to choose their own synesthesia color scheme. This is on the TODO list as well! “Horsey-color” that’s cute :)

I also think you’re spot on with the idea of having more nursery rhymes and folk songs… the current selection of songs are pretty complex. I’ll make a note on starting to find more of those, and perhaps having a “difficulty” rating.]]></wp:comment_content>
